# Nova first-run setup.
#
# Cloudflare reads this file during a "Deploy to Cloudflare" and asks you for each
# value below, then stores what you type as an encrypted Worker secret.
#
# IMPORTANT: this release does NOT lock first-run setup behind a claim token. A freshly
# deployed panel has no admin password yet, and /install is a public page, so whoever
# opens it first is the one who sets the password. There is no server-side check that
# stops someone else from claiming it during that window.
#
# So, to stay safe:
#   - If you install with the Telegram bot, it claims the panel for you automatically the
#     moment it deploys and hands you the password, so there is no open window.
#   - If you deploy by hand, open /install and set your admin password IMMEDIATELY after
#     the deploy finishes, before sharing the address with anyone.
#
# You can never be locked out of your own panel: you own the Worker, and the password
# lives in your own D1/KV, which you control from the Cloudflare dashboard under
# Workers & Pages > your worker > Settings > Variables and Secrets.
#
# NOVA_CLAIM_TOKEN is reserved for a future build that will enforce a first-run claim
# gate. This build does not read it, so setting it has no effect yet.
NOVA_CLAIM_TOKEN=
